---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/13-01/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/13-01/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/13-01/',photo='https://www.zaquant.uni-stuttgart.de/news-events/Zeiss-Gemini-560-ultrahigh-resolution-SEM-moved-to-the-ZAQuant/',family='https://asset-downloads.zeiss.com/catalogs/download/mic/d08dcd2e-6ec0-41a0-8e53-020b37baad5f/EN_product-info_GeminiSEM_Family_rel-3_4.pdf';
const display=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+String(v)).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="ZEISS GeminiSEM 560 passive grating" subtitle="" description="Inspect a metric GeminiSEM 560 exterior and compare two locked digital grating references." wide={true}>
<article id="g560" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/13-01/">← Equipment 13-01</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#g560-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">13-01 / ZEISS GeminiSEM 560 / Locked synthetic grating</p><h2>ZEISS GeminiSEM 560</h2><p>Look around the closed Gemini 3 exterior, then compare two stored grayscale grating patterns. Their 2 µm and 1 µm projected pitches differ by a factor of two. The instrument is a documentary model only.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect exterior and desk</h3><div id="g560-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Chamber','Viewer'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="g560-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="g560-model" aria-label="Orbitable GeminiSEM closed exterior and separate read-only inspection desk"></canvas><p id="g560-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click the left monitor to read the pattern or the brass desk button to switch its stored source. The enclosure is fixed. Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Choose a locked fixture</h3><div class="e-fields"><label>Stored source<select id="g560-frame"><option value="normal">Normal stock reference</option><option value="projected">Half-pitch projection reference</option></select></label></div>
<div class="e-row"><button id="g560-toggle" class="e-run" type="button">Compare other stored frame</button><button id="g560-reset" type="button">Restore normal reference</button></div><p id="g560-status" role="status">No synthetic frame loaded.</p><p id="g560-result" role="status">No pitch measured.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Read the grayscale calibration</h3><canvas id="g560-raster" width="240" height="96" aria-label="Locked synthetic 240 by 96 grayscale grating"></canvas><svg id="g560-scale" viewBox="0 0 240 15" role="img" aria-label="One micrometre equals 20 source pixels"><path d="M9 7h20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><text x="34" y="10" fill="currentColor" font-size="8">1 µm</text></svg>
<div class="e-row"><button id="g560-png" disabled>Raster PNG</button><button id="g560-json" disabled>Calibrated JSON</button></div><p>Both frames use the same synthetic 0.05 µm per pixel. The detector averages columns, finds rising crossings of 128 grayscale units and takes the median spacing. The projected pair has fixed metadata consistent with a cosine ratio of 0.5, not a change of actual stage orientation. PNG contains only the original pixels; JSON retains width, height, spacing, edge indices and provenance. <a href={a+'example-summary.json'}>Example metadata</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Documentary geometry</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original GeminiSEM 560 cabinet and witness desk"/><figcaption>Original silhouette based on the <a href={photo}>University of Stuttgart 560 installation photo</a>. The witness desk and software display are original.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original Gemini 3 upper column and fixed chamber"/><figcaption>The tall tower, upper collar and white lower cabinet distinguish the Gemini 3 exterior. See <a href={family}>ZEISS GeminiSEM family product information</a> for the feature comparison photo. No internals or usable access mechanism.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>The digital cabinet is about 0.91 m wide, 0.78 m deep at its base and 1.80 m high. These are photo-based modeling assumptions, not published mechanical tolerances. There is no beam, imaging/detector setup, chamber or specimen handling, scanning, biological procedure, or claim of resolution. The original register acceptance is addressed only by the passive image-spacing comparison, not a physical imaging model.</p></section>
<section id="g560-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'zeiss-geminisem-560.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} draw primitives; optional WebXR, physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/13-01/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#g560 header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#g560 h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#g560 section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#g560 button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#g560 button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#g560-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#g560-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#g560 table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#g560 td,#g560 th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#g560 figure{margin:0}#g560 img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#g560 caption{text-align:left}#g560 input,#g560 select,#g560 button{min-width:0}#g560 .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}#g560-raster,#g560-scale{display:block;width:min(100%,40rem);height:auto}#g560-raster{image-rendering:pixelated;background:#21272a}#g560-scale{margin:.15rem 0}</style>
